  "worked_solution": "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\u03ba(s)=\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(s)\u2016=\u2016{r}^{\u2033}(s)\u2016\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{\u2032}(s)$ and ${r}^{\u2033}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(s) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s+1}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3-4s}{5})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{3}{5},\\,-\\frac{4}{5}\u27e9 \\\\ {r}^{\u2033}(s) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{4}{5})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,0\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03ba(s) & =\u2016{r}^{\u2033}(s)\u2016 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
